## Source currency

Every exposure statement in this workpaper is a statement about the estate *as
observed by the source runs in this run*. Stale or interrupted source runs are
reported by the AWS and ASM/VM T7 checks and must be restated in the report body as a scope
limitation, not in a footnote. Where a scanner network scope has no credentialed
coverage (T2), patch-state statements about that scope are unauthenticated and
must be labelled as such.

## Exceptions & reperformance

Each fired row is an exception to its control. Why each exception matters and
what to reperform is documented per check under `docs/findings/`; dispositions
are recorded per finding. Every row carries a `record_locator` that names the
source rows behind it (ASM alert/rule id, VM finding id, IP, scanner name,
evidence bundle) so a reviewer can reperform the finding from the source export
without re-running the check.

